  "list_sessions": "List work sessions in this project and their projected status. Optional status and limit filters. Read-only.",
  "message_session": "Deliver a user-side fact into a work session. It is not a system instruction.\nintent \"answer\" delivers the original text as the user's answer to that session. If the admitted session is waiting on user input, the local runtime consumes the answer and resumes the existing task; otherwise it only appends the fact. It cannot approve a plan or resume a paused, superseded, or dependency-blocked session.\nintent \"amend\" relays the user's words as \"来自项目代理转达：用户说……\". If the session is waiting on the user, that relay is the answer and the session resumes. If the session is still running, the relay is applied when the next turn starts. Do not use amend to stop a session; call cancel_session for that.",
  "pause_objective": "Pause the owned objective. Its observations and history remain available. Paused objectives do not authorize automatic work.",
  "post_reply": "Post the visible reply in the project-agent conversation. replyTo lists the user messages this reply addresses. An unsolicited reply must set proactive to true. text is at most 2000 characters. sources name the sessions the reply is based on; a reply anchored to unreported completed tasks must cite them. Every source requires a statusClaims entry with its sessionId and current host status from get_session or the roster. Verification passing or auto policy does not imply accepted. Describe findings and blockers in text; the host supplies the actual task and acceptance state. On verification_required, run verify_session for the returned sessions, then retry with current status. On result_source_required or a status mismatch, use the returned sessionStates and revise the explanation before posting again. Optional question.options asks the user to choose.",
  "reprioritize_session": "Change an unfinished task priority to high, normal, or low. For high, provide anchorMessageId from this user turn explicitly requesting urgency or high priority. The host rejects wake turns, historical anchors, negated urgency and quoted urgency. Respect quoted task scope. This does not bypass dependencies, approval, isolation, or slot limits.",
  "resume_objective": "Resume or reopen the owned objective with an actual current canonical user_input anchor. A proposed objective needs explicit user confirmation; act still needs permission to act directly.",
